WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.434 --> 00:00:03.136
-Our next guest is a very funny
comedian and actor

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:04.838
who you know from
"The Carmichael Show"

00:00:04.838 --> 00:00:06.172
and films such as
"Neighbors"

00:00:06.172 --> 00:00:07.674
and "Transformers:
The Last Knight."

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:11.277
His latest special, "Rothaniel,"
is streaming on HBO Max.

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.678
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:15.915
-You can't talk about sex
with your parents.

00:00:15.915 --> 00:00:18.818
Not that anybody really wants
to, but you just can't.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:22.087
And you're -- you're only here
because your parents [bleep].

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:23.389
Isn't that kind of funny?

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:24.590
[ Laughter ]

00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:26.125
Your dad [bleep]
in your mom, and...

00:00:26.125 --> 00:00:27.660
[ Laughter ]

00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:29.762
...and you're here.

00:00:29.762 --> 00:00:32.265
But you got, like --
Have you ever been --

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.099
You ever been watching a movie
with your parents

00:00:34.099 --> 00:00:35.501
and, like,
a sex scene came on,

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:38.137
and you just got to be like,
"Nope. No, it's not."

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:44.444
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:47.513
Things that exist
but don't exist.

00:00:47.513 --> 00:00:49.181
It's things that, like,

00:00:49.181 --> 00:00:52.318
are right there,
hiding in plain sight.

00:00:52.318 --> 00:00:54.553
-Please welcome back
to the show our good friend

00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:56.089
Jerrod Carmichael,
everybody!

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:58.090
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:08.100 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:12.572 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:13.806
Welcome back.

00:01:13.806 --> 00:01:15.941
-Thank you very much.
-You were --

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:17.410
I saw you last Thursday.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:19.879
I stopped by in your dressing
room before you hosted "SNL."

00:01:19.879 --> 00:01:21.013
You did a wonderful job.

00:01:21.013 --> 00:01:22.415
Is it weird to be back
in the building...

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:23.916
-Thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:23.916 --> 00:01:25.852
Thank you.
-...so soon after?

00:01:25.852 --> 00:01:27.653
-Yeah.
I was saying on the elevator,

00:01:27.653 --> 00:01:29.488
it feels like coming back

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:32.191
to your old high school
a week after you graduate.

00:01:32.191 --> 00:01:34.260
-Yeah.
-And it's like I was going

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:36.329
to say hi, but I'm afraid
of everyone being like,

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.497
"What is he doing here?"
-Right.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.433
They might think,
"I think he doesn't understand

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:41.500
how it works."
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.136
"It's over.
It's over, bro."

00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.072
-They have moved on.
-I kind of miss it, though.

00:01:46.072 --> 00:01:48.374
Like, I would go back this week,
honestly, like,

00:01:48.374 --> 00:01:50.943
because it's like you spend
a week and it's a whirlwind

00:01:50.943 --> 00:01:53.846
and you figure it out
and, you know...

00:01:53.846 --> 00:01:55.414
You try to figure it out,

00:01:55.414 --> 00:01:57.316
and it's really fun
and exciting.

00:01:57.316 --> 00:01:59.686
It's like the best group
of people.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:01.954
Like, I understand everyone's
sincere goodbyes

00:02:01.954 --> 00:02:03.189
at the end of "SNL."

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:04.356
Like, people are like,
"Oh, it's like

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:05.859
the best week of my life."

00:02:05.859 --> 00:02:07.160
And you're like, "Oh, I get it."

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.862
It's like a lot of, like,
incredible professionals

00:02:09.862 --> 00:02:13.499
and, like, brilliant writers
and excellent cast,

00:02:13.499 --> 00:02:15.634
and it was
a beautiful experience.

00:02:15.634 --> 00:02:17.102
-Yeah, and everybody --
you know,

00:02:17.102 --> 00:02:19.571
the goal is to take care of you,
the host, and it's really --

00:02:19.571 --> 00:02:21.807
-Yeah.
-Even when I went back,

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:23.342
I'm like,
"Oh, this is really lovely.

00:02:23.342 --> 00:02:24.910
Everybody's thinking way
more about me now

00:02:24.910 --> 00:02:25.978
than when I worked here."

00:02:25.978 --> 00:02:28.081
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, that's nice.

00:02:28.081 --> 00:02:29.982
Yeah.
Yeah, that is nice.

00:02:29.982 --> 00:02:32.818
It's what I imagine, like, the,
you know, the first week of,

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:34.787
like, foster care feels like.

00:02:34.787 --> 00:02:38.324
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.194
It's all, like, you know,
spaghetti and...

00:02:41.194 --> 00:02:43.963
[ Laughs ]
-But it's fast, right?

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.899
So you don't have a lot of time
to think about "SNL,"

00:02:46.899 --> 00:02:49.368
but you do have a lot of time
to think about a special.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.770
And this is such a brilliant
special,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:54.407
and it's obviously so personal.

00:02:54.407 --> 00:02:56.642
And I want to ask, because
you've done specials before

00:02:56.642 --> 00:02:59.078
and you're going to do this one,
what are the --

00:02:59.078 --> 00:03:01.480
Because, you know,
the headline of the special

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.816
is you come out
as gay in this special.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:06.286
-Yeah.
-And what is the --

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.553
When you embark on this special,

00:03:07.553 --> 00:03:09.255
what is the decision-making
process to be like,

00:03:09.255 --> 00:03:11.491
"This is what this one's
going to be about"?

00:03:13.726 --> 00:03:15.494
-I couldn't think
of anything else.

00:03:15.494 --> 00:03:17.263
I mean, that was like...

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:19.165
[ Laughter ]

00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:21.668
I'm so gay, I just couldn't...

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.835
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.835 --> 00:03:24.971
Like, what else?
No, don't clap.

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:26.539
I -- I actually --

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:27.707
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.709
Please, thank you very --
thank you very much.

00:03:30.709 --> 00:03:33.780
I have to -- I keep saying
I'm gay in New York

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.550
and people keep clapping,
and it was so nice.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.352
-Yeah.
-But it's like, all right.

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.220
-Yeah, because you've been --
do you realize, you're like,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:43.723
"Oh, you can't bank it
when you go somewhere else"?

00:03:43.723 --> 00:03:45.057
-Yeah, yeah.

00:03:45.057 --> 00:03:47.193
Y'all are just building me up,
and I can't --

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:51.196
Like, life doesn't work
like that for the rest of it.

00:03:51.196 --> 00:03:52.665
It's very kind.

00:03:52.665 --> 00:03:56.168
I'm learning how to receive
love, and I actually need that.

00:03:56.168 --> 00:03:58.771
I joke about it
because it's a --

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:03.242
it's a thing I'm learning now,
like, in life as a man.

00:04:03.242 --> 00:04:04.443
And it's definitely --

00:04:04.443 --> 00:04:08.514
I need it to,
like, supplement...

00:04:08.514 --> 00:04:11.483
I think there's kind of
a little bit of a rift

00:04:11.483 --> 00:04:12.651
with me and my family,

00:04:12.651 --> 00:04:16.288
and, like, you know,
that kind of core tribe.

00:04:16.288 --> 00:04:23.528
So, like, I've been receiving
love from strangers...

00:04:23.528 --> 00:04:25.098
sexually and nonsexually.

00:04:25.098 --> 00:04:29.202
[ Laughter ]
-It's nice to have a balance.

00:04:29.202 --> 00:04:33.506
-But it's been --
it's been really nice.

00:04:33.506 --> 00:04:36.675
I had a crazy, crazy drive here.

00:04:36.675 --> 00:04:37.910
Like, a crazy drive here.

00:04:37.910 --> 00:04:39.746
I talked to my parents
for the first time.

00:04:39.746 --> 00:04:41.547
-Oh, now this,
I'm fascinated by this

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:46.385
because you talk especially
about the fact that, you know,

00:04:46.385 --> 00:04:48.554
you did not come out
to your mom in the special.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.656
You'd come out to her before.

00:04:50.656 --> 00:04:51.757
-Yeah, well, kind of.

00:04:51.757 --> 00:04:54.026
I have to renew it.

00:04:54.026 --> 00:04:55.828
Like, if -- [ Chuckles ]

00:04:55.828 --> 00:04:59.098
Like, my mom practices a lot
of cognitive dissonance with it,

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.367
and so it's like --
or denial, rather,

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:06.038
and so I have to come out,
like, every other conversation.

00:05:06.038 --> 00:05:08.107
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.743
-So how did the conversation go?

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:12.945
-Uh...

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:14.380
I don't know.

00:05:14.380 --> 00:05:16.249
I'm trying to -- what's
the television version of it?

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:19.118
[ Laughter ]

00:05:19.118 --> 00:05:20.987
You know, I called in the car.

00:05:20.987 --> 00:05:22.788
I was nervous.
She called.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:25.357
Today's my birthday, and --
-Happy birthday, buddy.

00:05:25.357 --> 00:05:27.160
-Oh, thank you.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:27.160 --> 00:05:28.394
[ Indistinct ]
See, that's too much.

00:05:28.394 --> 00:05:30.296
That's already so much.

00:05:30.296 --> 00:05:32.598
-Now, I will notice that was,
like, twice as much applause

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:33.666
that they gave you
for being gay.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.134
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:05:35.134 --> 00:05:39.038
Maybe it's more my birthday
than gay I am.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:41.640
Bad sentence.
Anyway, um...

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.144
I was nervous because
it was a lot in the special,

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:49.081
a lot of things that
I was afraid to say to her.

00:05:49.081 --> 00:05:54.020
And I said it in the special,
and so she called,

00:05:54.020 --> 00:05:57.856
and I was nervous because...

00:05:57.856 --> 00:06:00.593
my mom and my family can be
very polite,

00:06:00.593 --> 00:06:03.095
and we can kind of,
like, smile.

00:06:03.095 --> 00:06:04.964
I don't know if any of your
families are like that,

00:06:04.964 --> 00:06:07.766
but, like, just kind of smile
through things

00:06:07.766 --> 00:06:09.668
and not talk about things.

00:06:09.668 --> 00:06:12.237
There's a lot of elephants
in the room.

00:06:12.237 --> 00:06:14.640
I think my family lives inside
an elephant, actually.

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:15.675
[ Laughter ]

00:06:15.675 --> 00:06:19.545
I think the elephant
is the room.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.380
And we're great performers.

00:06:21.380 --> 00:06:23.348
[ Chuckles ]

00:06:23.348 --> 00:06:25.918
And I was afraid
that the call would just be

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:27.954
about my birthday...

00:06:27.954 --> 00:06:33.092
when I feel like there's
obviously more pressing matters.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:39.431
And it was an emotional call,
and she expressed a lot of love.

00:06:39.431 --> 00:06:41.267
So did my dad.

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:44.804
They made very strong calls
for peace.

00:06:44.804 --> 00:06:47.106
So it sounds like news
about Ukraine.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:50.476
Like, "We just want peace, son."

00:06:50.476 --> 00:06:53.112
Like, that's what -- they're
just, like, praying for peace

00:06:53.112 --> 00:06:55.148
and, you know...

00:06:55.148 --> 00:06:59.017
And it was almost very nice.

00:06:59.017 --> 00:07:00.419
It was very dramatic.

00:07:00.419 --> 00:07:04.757
I was going by billboards of me,
like, as the call was going,

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:05.958
and like sirens are going off.

00:07:05.958 --> 00:07:07.426
It was really weird.

00:07:07.426 --> 00:07:09.895
And it was --
it was almost very nice

00:07:09.895 --> 00:07:13.432
until, you know, my mom said,
like, you know,

00:07:13.432 --> 00:07:16.969
"I just -- these sins
are tearing the family apart."

00:07:16.969 --> 00:07:21.207
And it just speaks to the...

00:07:21.207 --> 00:07:27.112
kind of the core of the problem,
you know, that there's this...

00:07:27.112 --> 00:07:30.950
insurmountable mountain that
we can't really get over.

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:32.951
[ Chuckles ]

00:07:32.951 --> 00:07:34.653
And it was real dramatic.

00:07:34.653 --> 00:07:35.822
And then the driver was like,

00:07:35.822 --> 00:07:37.189
"All right,
it's time to come out,"

00:07:37.189 --> 00:07:38.991
and then I got out of the car,
and now I'm here.

00:07:38.991 --> 00:07:40.126
[ Laughter ]

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:41.593
So that's where I'm at.

00:07:41.593 --> 00:07:43.862
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.862 --> 00:07:45.031
-What's up with y'all, though?

00:07:45.031 --> 00:07:47.166
Y'all good?
Everybody cool, though?

00:07:47.166 --> 00:07:48.701
[ Chuckles ]
I'm all right.

00:07:48.701 --> 00:07:49.936
I'm all right, I'm good.
[ Applause ]

00:07:49.936 --> 00:07:53.672
My bad for bringing...this.

00:07:53.672 --> 00:07:57.209
-You mentioned about
not having --

00:07:57.209 --> 00:07:58.644
in the special,
in the body of the special,

00:07:58.644 --> 00:08:00.546
about not having sort of had
that breakthrough with your mom.

00:08:00.546 --> 00:08:02.281
But you did mention
near the end of it

00:08:02.281 --> 00:08:03.982
you knew she would watch it.

00:08:03.982 --> 00:08:05.084
-Yeah.
-I thought that was --

00:08:05.084 --> 00:08:06.451
that was a really lovely thing
to hear

00:08:06.451 --> 00:08:08.988
because obviously it seems like

00:08:08.988 --> 00:08:10.789
you might feel, like,
some emotional limbo,

00:08:10.789 --> 00:08:12.358
but you also knew
she loved you enough

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:14.527
she wasn't going to not
watch the special.

00:08:14.527 --> 00:08:16.061
Is that something --
has she always engaged

00:08:16.061 --> 00:08:18.097
with your work
like that as a fan?

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:21.533
-Yeah, well, that and they're
all signed into my HBO Max.

00:08:21.533 --> 00:08:23.002
So...
-Yeah.

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:24.336
[ Laughter ]

00:08:24.336 --> 00:08:25.971
So it's like,
"Continue watching."

00:08:25.971 --> 00:08:27.573
-It was on "Up next."

00:08:27.573 --> 00:08:32.611
[ Laughter ]

00:08:32.611 --> 00:08:36.615
Uh, yeah, like, you know,
obviously just having a son

00:08:36.615 --> 00:08:38.283
on television,
you know, means --

00:08:38.283 --> 00:08:40.786
I told her I was getting out
a car coming here.

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:45.724
It's all kind of odd and surreal
because it's playing out like...

00:08:45.724 --> 00:08:46.959
she'll watch this.

00:08:46.959 --> 00:08:50.696
You know, this is --
You know, it's all...

00:08:50.696 --> 00:08:52.197
You know.

00:08:52.197 --> 00:08:54.800
-It's also thematically...

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.602
It seemed like the way
you approached it

00:08:56.602 --> 00:08:59.639
was there was no way
to do this special

00:08:59.639 --> 00:09:02.841
telling half or 75%
or 80% of the truth --

00:09:02.841 --> 00:09:04.777
and not just your own truth,
but a lot of --

00:09:04.777 --> 00:09:07.580
you know, again, if there's
a theme being, like, secrets,

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.948
there were other secrets
about people in your family.

00:09:09.948 --> 00:09:14.287
How have they responded
to that element of it?

00:09:14.287 --> 00:09:18.157
-Um...

00:09:18.157 --> 00:09:19.558
Measured slowly.

00:09:19.558 --> 00:09:25.998
I got a really great text
from my dad, um, uh...

00:09:25.998 --> 00:09:28.234
just really saying

00:09:28.234 --> 00:09:29.734
that he wanted
to take responsibility

00:09:29.734 --> 00:09:32.071
for trauma he caused.

00:09:32.071 --> 00:09:35.274
He apologized
for a lot of the chaos.

00:09:35.274 --> 00:09:36.409
Like, "I'm sorry for the chaos."

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:39.145
My dad speaks very dramatically.

00:09:39.145 --> 00:09:40.379
It's nice, though.

00:09:40.379 --> 00:09:42.247
[ Chuckles ]

00:09:42.247 --> 00:09:44.983
And, uh...

00:09:44.983 --> 00:09:46.385
He -- He's responded.

00:09:46.385 --> 00:09:48.954
I don't think it's things that
he's ever said out loud.

00:09:48.954 --> 00:09:50.790
It's odd.
It's like...

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.457
I was, um...

00:09:52.457 --> 00:09:54.559
I think kind of speaking
for my family,

00:09:54.559 --> 00:09:58.898
in many ways, just...

00:09:58.898 --> 00:10:03.835
trying to free myself, at least,
and hopefully my father.

00:10:03.835 --> 00:10:07.339
Not to sound like Odysseus,
you know, but --

00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:10.642
but, like,
just trying to...

00:10:10.642 --> 00:10:12.010
Yeah.
Yeah, just -- they --

00:10:12.010 --> 00:10:14.813
They've responded, like...

00:10:14.813 --> 00:10:16.081
It's slowly coming in.

00:10:16.081 --> 00:10:17.515
It's slowly coming in, I think.

00:10:17.515 --> 00:10:19.251
-I also was fascinated...

00:10:19.251 --> 00:10:21.320
Not to ask a process question,
but, you know,

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.688
I often think
of stand-up specials

00:10:22.688 --> 00:10:24.256
as different tracks
on an album,

00:10:24.256 --> 00:10:26.825
whereas this seemed like
one piece of music.

00:10:26.825 --> 00:10:28.093
-Yeah.
-And I was wondering, like,

00:10:28.093 --> 00:10:30.862
how did you even work it
on stage?

00:10:30.862 --> 00:10:34.499
Because it almost felt like it
always had to be a whole.

00:10:34.499 --> 00:10:36.835
And I should note that,
you know,

00:10:36.835 --> 00:10:38.637
it's an hour,
like most specials.

00:10:38.637 --> 00:10:39.972
It went by very quickly for me,

00:10:39.972 --> 00:10:43.308
even though it was really
intense and far weightier

00:10:43.308 --> 00:10:44.910
than what you expect
from a stand-up special.

00:10:44.910 --> 00:10:48.313
But because it had
this real lyric quality,

00:10:48.313 --> 00:10:50.315
which I think is both a credit
to you and Bo Burnham,

00:10:50.315 --> 00:10:52.150
who did a beautiful job
directing it.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:53.886
So how did you ever work on it?

00:10:53.886 --> 00:10:56.522
Or was this a piece of comedy
that you didn't work

00:10:56.522 --> 00:10:58.991
as much
as maybe previous specials?

00:10:58.991 --> 00:11:00.559
-I actually -- it's odd.

00:11:00.559 --> 00:11:04.529
It happened faster than
my previous specials, in a way.

00:11:04.529 --> 00:11:08.734
This happened from December,
like right before Christmas.

00:11:08.734 --> 00:11:14.006
I was staying with Bo,
and I was actually sad

00:11:14.006 --> 00:11:15.507
because this dude
didn't text me back,

00:11:15.507 --> 00:11:18.009
and so then I threw myself
in to work, so...

00:11:18.009 --> 00:11:19.545
Thanks, I guess.
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:19.545 --> 00:11:21.246
[ Laughter ]

00:11:21.246 --> 00:11:24.883
-And just started going up
and just talking about things

00:11:24.883 --> 00:11:26.184
I hadn't talked about before.

00:11:26.184 --> 00:11:30.456
And, at first, they came out
very free associative,

00:11:30.456 --> 00:11:33.926
but kind of the same rule
in my work now

00:11:33.926 --> 00:11:37.062
that I have in therapy is
just, like, you know, don't lie.

00:11:37.062 --> 00:11:40.299
It would be a waste of time.

00:11:40.299 --> 00:11:43.034
And so it kind of came
together quickly.

00:11:43.034 --> 00:11:45.771
Like, the narrative and the arc
and the story of it

00:11:45.771 --> 00:11:48.774
just kind of started
making sense as I was saying it.

00:11:48.774 --> 00:11:51.943
But it happened --
it happened --

00:11:51.943 --> 00:11:53.245
I went to various cities,

00:11:53.245 --> 00:11:56.682
Atlanta and San Francisco
and Austin,

00:11:56.682 --> 00:12:01.620
and worked it out
and just me alone on stage,

00:12:01.620 --> 00:12:04.389
and audiences
kind of everywhere,

00:12:04.389 --> 00:12:08.594
kind of would chime in
and, like, react in a way

00:12:08.594 --> 00:12:14.966
that I had never felt
before as a performer.

00:12:14.966 --> 00:12:18.537
-Yeah, but there's moments
where the audience sort of

00:12:18.537 --> 00:12:21.073
asks you questions
that are very thoughtful.

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:23.475
So it's like the opposite
of heckling, right?

00:12:23.475 --> 00:12:25.844
-Yeah.
-They are actually --

00:12:25.844 --> 00:12:28.180
In a weird way, I felt like,
"Oh, they're channeling

00:12:28.180 --> 00:12:29.882
exactly what
I'm thinking at this moment,"

00:12:29.882 --> 00:12:31.083
and then you're
responding to them.

00:12:31.083 --> 00:12:32.885
Did that happen
everywhere you did it?

00:12:32.885 --> 00:12:34.186
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:12:34.186 --> 00:12:39.224
In most places, it would be
just moments where, um...

00:12:39.224 --> 00:12:40.892
I would get these thoughtful --

00:12:40.892 --> 00:12:44.463
I felt like I was
giving the audiences

00:12:44.463 --> 00:12:45.631
the truth and all of me.

00:12:45.631 --> 00:12:47.032
There was always this wall.

00:12:47.032 --> 00:12:51.470
I used to kind of present
this brash persona as a comic,

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.771
and I --

00:12:52.771 --> 00:12:55.073
I had to accept how much
I needed the audience,

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:56.508
like, how important it is.

00:12:56.508 --> 00:12:59.345
Like, I'm asking you
to share this with me,

00:12:59.345 --> 00:13:02.781
and I'm sharing more
of myself with audiences,

00:13:02.781 --> 00:13:06.485
and I feel like they responded
in kind, and it was beautiful.

00:13:06.485 --> 00:13:08.954
It's been very beautiful, and it
makes me want to perform more.

00:13:08.954 --> 00:13:12.291
And, uh...yeah.
Yeah.

00:13:12.291 --> 00:13:14.926
-Well, it is --
it's really something to watch.

00:13:14.926 --> 00:13:18.730
I also want to say, for anybody
who hasn't seen yet,

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:20.865
the payoff at the end
completely caught me off guard.

00:13:20.865 --> 00:13:23.268
I am so ashamed that I did not
see the last joke coming.

00:13:23.268 --> 00:13:24.669
-Really?
-Yeah! I can't believe it.

00:13:24.669 --> 00:13:26.705
-Really?
-It made me laugh so hard.

00:13:26.705 --> 00:13:29.240
-That'll be -- [ Laughs ]
Bo will like that.

00:13:29.240 --> 00:13:30.709
I'll tell him.
[ Laughs ]

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:33.845
-And, yeah, it's really
something to see,

00:13:33.845 --> 00:13:35.647
and thank you so much
for making time for us today.

00:13:35.647 --> 00:13:37.449
-Thanks for having me.
Thank you, guys.

00:13:37.449 --> 00:13:40.018
-You guys,
that's Jerrod Carmichael.

00:13:40.018 --> 00:13:42.588
"Rothaniel," streaming now
on HBO Max.

